The advantages of field-oriented control can be summarized as follows:
● High efficiency obtained by aligning the stator and rotor flows to generate excellent
torque production by the machine;
● High dynamic response obtained by controlling the quantities (voltages, currents and
fluxes) in module and phase;
● Low torque ripple, as the stator field is continuously updated according to the position of
the rotor field;
● Independent control of flux and torque, as in direct current machines;
● High dynamic range through weakening operation;
● High torque and low starting current.
